<title>USA: CENFED Financial Corp Q4 net income rises.</title>
<headline>CENFED Financial Corp Q4 net income rises.</headline>
<dateline>PASADENA, Calif. 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>3 Mos ended 12/31    12 Mos ended 12/31</p>
<p>				 1996	1995	 1996	1995</p>
<p> Net interest income $ 12,397    $10,963     $51,159  $38,485</p>
<p> Prov for loan losses  (1,500)    (1,000)     (8,050)  (2,900)</p>
<p>Net after provisions</p>
<p>  for loan losses	10,897	9,963	43,109   35,585</p>
<p> Non-interest income    2,246	2,304	12,633    7,254</p>
<p> Operating expense     (9,079)    (8,966)    (44,067) (33,151)</p>
<p>Earnings before taxes and</p>
<p>   extraordinary item   4,064	3,301	11,675    9,688</p>
<p>  Income taxes	   (1,336)    (1,002)	   27   (2,491)</p>
<p> Extraordinary item	  --	   --	 (364)	 --</p>
<p>Net earnings/EPS 2,728/0.51 2,299/0.45 11,338/2.17 7,197/1.42</p>
<p>NOTE: Core EPS on a primary-share basis were $0.60 in Q4 1996 and $0.48 in Q4 1995.</p>
<p>&quot;Core earnings&quot; exclude gains and losses on sales of investments and mortgage-backed securities, results of real estate operations and nonrecurring adjustments such as the deposit insurance recapitalization premium paid in 1996 and severance costs associated with discontinued lines of business.  </p>
<p>All earnings-per- share figures include the effect of a 10% stock dividend distributed by the company in May 1996.</p>
